May that day be darkness;
may the Lord above not seek it out,
and may no brightness come upon it.

May the stars of that night be darkened;
may it wait and not come into light,
and may it not see the morning star rising,

I stood up and did not recognize it;
I looked, and there was no form before my eyes,
but I heard a breeze and a voice:

as for those who inhabit houses of clay,
from which we ourselves also are, of the same clay,
He struck them as one does a moth.

For the righteous will eat what they gathered,
and they themselves will not be rescued from evils;
may their strength be drained away.

Behold, we have searched these things out in this way;
these are the things we have heard.
But know for yourself whether you have done anything.”

For the Lord’s arrows are in my body;
their fury drinks up my blood.
When I begin to speak, they stab me.

So I too will not restrain my mouth;
I will speak in my distress;
held fast, I will disclose the bitterness of my soul.

for they have been handed over into an ungodly person’s hands.
He covers the faces of its judges;
if it is not He, who is it?’

But deliverance will abandon them,
for their hope is destruction,
and the eyes of the ungodly will waste away.”

Thou didst put my foot in a restraint
and watch all my works;
Thou didst reach to the roots of my feet.

May he lodge in deserted cities
and enter uninhabited houses;
what those people prepared, others will carry away.

He will conceive pains in the womb;
empty things will result for him,
and his belly will bear deceit.”

Dealing in anger, He cast me down
and gnashed His teeth at me;
the arrows of His raiders fell upon me.

He sprang upon me with points of eyes;
He struck my jaw with a sharp point,
and together they rushed down upon me.

While I was at peace, He scattered me;
He took me by the hair and tore me apart,
and set me up like a target.

They surrounded me with spears,
striking my kidneys without sparing;
they poured my gall onto the earth.

My brothers withdrew from me;
they recognized strangers rather than me,
and my friends became merciless.

things that I know with myself,
that my eye has seen, and no other;
everything has been accomplished within my breast.

you too must beware of a covering,
for wrath will come upon the lawless,
and then they will know where their substance is.”

For when he thinks he has become firmly established,
then he will perish utterly;
those who saw him will say, ‘Where is he?’

May an arrow pass through his body,
and may lightning bolts walk among his dwellings;
terrors are upon him.

May every darkness remain for him;
an unkindled fire will consume him,
and may a stranger harm his house.

Nevertheless, even the lamp of the ungodly will be extinguished;
overthrow will come upon them,
and pangs will grip them because of wrath.

The pebbles of the stream became sweet to him;
every human will go after him,
and those before him are countless.

They departed like donkeys in a field,
going out beyond me to their own activity;
bread became sweet to him for the young.

People were driven from a city and their own houses;
the life of infants groaned loudly.
Why has He Himself not made an inspection of these things?

While they were upon the earth, they did not recognize it;
they did not know the road of righteousness
or walk in its paths.

He dug into houses in darkness;
by day they sealed themselves in;
they did not recognize light.

For his exaltation mistreated many;
he withered like mallow in scorching heat,
or like an ear of grain that falls of itself from the stalk.

I chose their way and sat as ruler;
I encamped like a king among lightly equipped soldiers,
in the manner of one consoling sufferers.”

At the right hand of a shoot they rose;
they stretched out their foot
and made roads against me, the paths of their destruction.

He struck me with His missiles;
He has dealt with me as He wishes;
I am befouled with pains.

My pains return;
my hope went away like wind,
and my salvation like a cloud.

If my foot turned from the road,
if my heart followed my eye,
or if I touched gifts with my hands,

Elihu son of Barachel the Buzite replied:
“I am younger in time, and you are older;
therefore I kept quiet, afraid to announce my own knowledge to you.

Give ear to my words;
for I will speak while you listen,
until you examine words.

I will also direct my understanding toward you;
and behold, there was no one among you refuting Job,
answering his words,

He will hold him back from falling into death,
and renew his body like plaster upon a wall,
and fill his bones with marrow;

When he prays to the Lord, it will be acceptable to Him;
he will enter with a pure face, with confession,
and He will return righteousness to humans.

will He repay it on your terms?
For you will reject it, for you will choose, not I;
speak what you have known.

so that we may not add to our sins;
lawlessness will be reckoned against us
as we speak many words before the Lord.”

He will not take His eyes from a righteous person;
with kings upon a throne
He will seat them for victory, and they will be raised high.

Moreover, He deceived you out of an enemy’s mouth;
an abyss, a pouring-down beneath it;
and your table descended, full of fatness.

Let your mind not willingly turn you away
from the plea of the powerless who are in constraint,
and all those strengthening might.

After it a voice will cry out;
He will thunder with the voice of His violence,
and He will not exchange them, because he will hear His voice.

Light is not visible to everyone;
it shines afar in the old things,
like the light from Him upon clouds.

We do not find another like Him in strength;
He judges righteous things—
do you not think He hears?
